<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - Conrail up on reported pact.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - Conrail up on reported pact.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conrail Inc shares rallied in pre-open trade Monday as buyers acted on news of a possible agreement to end the four-month fight between CSX Corp and Norfolk Southern Corp to acquire Conrail.</p>
<p>Conrail stock climbed to 111 per share, up from 104-1/2 at Friday's New York Stock Exchange close, traders said.</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal reported the battling CSX and Norfolk are close to a deal whereby CSX would pay $115 per share for Conrail, or $10.5 billion.</p>
<p>Norfolk then would acquire almost half of Conrail's routes, according to the newspaper.</p>
</text>
